napshot projection (not only spy-observed effect counts) for at least one CLI and one Python operation.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7437,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Add consumer-level metamorphic and effect-spy tests.'","'proven by call-count tests through production entry points'","'produce existing effects' — but no explicit live end-to-end write assertion that the defaulted composition path performs a real store write, so offline/spy-only coverage could go green while the live threaded path is broken"],"finding":"This is a cutover that makes snapshot-derived composition the default resolution path for CLI, MCP, and Python store writes, yet the acceptance relies on 'effect-spy tests' and 'call-count tests' that may verify effects only through spies intercepting before the real lock/subprocess/network/store boundary. The plan does not state an end-to-end/live acceptance that a real store write actually occurs through the newly-threaded projection.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f451e1063a0ddc769","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section / Acceptance Criteria bullets 1 and 5","norm_id":"n23a7ac1b7dad5d4f","priority":0.2063,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A store-write operation composes and threads the projection correctly under spies (green), but the real store append through the threaded context is mis-wired and never asserted end-to-end, so the cutover closes green while live writes are broken."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'A representative CLI and Python store write executes end-to-end through the threaded projection and produces a real on-disk ticket/event, asserted against stored content, not only via effect spies.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_con